# Wave W17-M (Route 109): bay rock — harbour-mouth rock: two rounded warm-brown boulders standing where the bay meets the open sea, worn smooth by the harbour water, foam collar at their feet, the sea baked in around them (design: the harbour mouth under Fairhaven’s pier). Route 109’s own rock — round harbour boulders, split from Route 108’s rib-reef and Route 106’s spired crag.
